# TEST: a mass-changing surface reaction on a spinning body of revolution
#
# every hit flips the species between A and B, whose masses differ by 2x, so
# the collision impulse is mpost*v - mpre*vpre with two different masses and
# the recoil correction must take the matrix branch of the axisymmetric kmat
#
# the wall is specular and the body spins, which is what makes this test the
# azimuthal channel and not just the axial one: specular reflection leaves
# the azimuthal velocity RELATIVE TO THE WALL unchanged, so the lab v_theta
# is unchanged too, and the azimuthal impulse is exactly
#   (mpost - mpre) * v_theta
# which is non-zero only because the mass changed.  the body answers it
# through kmat[2][2] = r^2/ixx and its spin responds
#
# ixx is small enough that the body's spin answers visibly: the azimuthal
# impulse has zero mean for a thermal gas, so the spin random-walks rather
# than drifting, and over the run it covers about +-15% while the gas
# carries the balance
#
# the gas is given a net axial drift so that sum(m vx) does not sit on a
# near-total cancellation: with vstream 0 the sum is a random walk about
# zero, its magnitude is smaller than that of its own terms, and the
# reduction-order noise of an MPI sum then swamps any relative measure of
# the closure
#
# both exact invariants must hold to round-off, with the per-particle mass
# taken from the CURRENT species so the sums follow the reactions:
#   fnum sum(m vx)     + M vcm_x   + 0.5 dt fx
#   fnum sum(m r vth)  + ixx w_x   + 0.5 dt tx
# neither is conserved by the reaction itself -- an exchange between species
# of different mass does not conserve gas momentum -- but the impulse the
# body is given is exactly the momentum the gas lost, so the sum is

seed	    	    12345

variable            dist index 0
if "${dist} == 1" then "global surfs explicit/distributed"
dimension   	    2
boundary            p ar p

create_box  	    0 1 0 0.3 -0.5 0.5
create_grid 	    20 6 1
balance_grid        rcb cell

global		    nrho 1.0 fnum 0.001

species		    air2.species A B
mixture		    air A B vstream 100.0 0 0 temp 500.0

read_surf           adata.cylinder group body
surf_collide	    1 specular
surf_react          r1 prob exch2.surf
surf_modify         all collide 1 react r1
collide             none

timestep 	    1.0e-5


global              rigid yes

fix		    1 rigid body single body &
		    mass 1.0e-22 com 0.5 0 0 vcom 0 0 0 &
		    moi 5.0e-28 1.0e-24 1.0e-24 0 0 0 angmom 5.0e-25 0 0

create_particles    air n 20000

variable            px particle mass*vx
variable            lx particle mass*y*vz
compute             rp reduce sum v_px
compute             rl reduce sum v_lx

stats		    200
stats_style         step np c_rp c_rl f_1[4] f_1[13] f_1[7] f_1[10] f_1
stats_modify        format float %20.14e
run 		    2000
